  nonce: c2d6  # c2d6
  message: "Re-confirmed on dev 95c0ff7b93 by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (verifier read the code): - jackson_dispatch.py: (metadata; runtime effect unverified) L433-434 `# CNF: Jackson is Java-only.` / `depends_on=[[\"java\"]]` contradicts the code, which accepts `sym.language not in {\"java\", \"kotlin\", \"scala\"}` (L329, L376) and builds collisions over `languages=frozenset({\"java\", \"kotlin\", \"scala\"})` (L451). Per registry.py:57-59, `depends_on` only drives the PREREQUISITE_ABSENT stamp on an unexplained run, so the likely effect is a wrong attribution on Kotlin/Scala-only repos. I did not reproduce that end to end -- evidence: the quoted lines. - kafka_streams_dispatch.py: depends_on names only java, but the body scans kotlin and scala too -- evidence: L357-358 `# CNF: Kafka Streams API is Java-only.` / `depends_on=[[\"java\"]],` vs L383 `if sym.language not in {\"java\", \"kotlin\", \"scala\"}:` (same at L273, L319). The registry's wrapper (registry.py:847-850) stamps `PREREQUISITE_ABSENT` when `_blocked_prerequisite_clauses(ctx)` is non-empty. `prerequisite_absent_clauses` (pass_silence.py:671-675) fires when every literal in a clause is absent and at least one is absent for a toolchain reason. So a Kotlin/Scala-only repo whose java grammar is toolchain-skipped gets a false PREREQUISITE_ABSENT. A repo whose kotlin/scala analyzer is toolchain-blocked is never flagged. Fix: `depends_on=[[\"java\", \"kotlin\", \"scala\"]]` and drop the \"Java-only\" comment."  # c2d6
